capability env/read  the value of one environment variable
  heroes  os.env
  go      os.Getenv, os.LookupEnv
  rust    env::var
  python  os.getenv, os.environ (an item read)
  note    unset is `not_found` and never "", where Go's Getenv answers "" for both; a default is `.default(v)`. An empty name, or one holding `=` or a zero byte, is `invalid`: all three answer absent (observed), but no system can hold such a name, so asking for one is a mistake the caller can see

capability env/read-bytes  the value of one environment variable as the bytes the system holds
  heroes  os.env_bytes
  go      -
  rust    env::var_os
  python  os.getenvb, os.environb (an item read)
  note    `env` fails `not_text` for a value that is not UTF-8; this one never does

capability env/read-all  every variable of the environment at once, in the system's order
  heroes  os.env_all
  go      os.Environ
  rust    env::vars
  python  os.environ
  note    a map in the system's order; an entry with no `=`, or with an empty name (Windows' `=C:`), is left out as Rust and Python leave it, where Go's Environ hands every entry as it stands; a name standing twice keeps its first value, the one `env` reads. A name or value that is not UTF-8 is `not_text`, where Rust's vars panics

