  note    one text: on POSIX `uname`'s release, the kernel's, Python's platform.release (observed "27.2.0", the same as `uname -r`); on Darwin that is the kernel's number, not macOS's own, which Python's mac_ver answers (observed "27.2"); on Windows `major.minor.build` from `RtlGetVersion`, which no manifest changes. The rest of `uname`, the edition, the distribution's release file and the C library's version are not offered

