capability stop/catch  Ctrl-C and SIGTERM made a stop the program asks about
  heroes  os.catch_stop
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    The platform layer's stop (spec § 13): every call of the library that waits on the system, a socket's, a serial port's, a poller's, a watcher's or a channel's, fails `stopped`. Its C is `hero_net.h`'s, bound by the floor `os/hero_stop`; it stood in `net` until the coherence review's D18 (2026-11-21), so a program that reads a serial port now ends on Ctrl-C without naming `net`

